1
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:14,910
How is Rafilia?

2
00:00:15,630 --> 00:00:16,820
She's fine.

3
00:00:17,310 --> 00:00:19,290
She was probably tense this whole time.

4
00:00:19,290 --> 00:00:20,660
She fell asleep.

5
00:00:22,310 --> 00:00:25,460
Brother, sorry for worrying you.

6
00:00:25,460 --> 00:00:29,410
No need to thank me.
 I'm glad your daughter is safe.

7
00:00:30,470 --> 00:00:31,260
Yes.

8
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:06,080
RAVISEL'S INTENTIONS

9
00:02:06,350 --> 00:02:08,410
Is Rafilia all right?

10
00:02:08,860 --> 00:02:09,730
Yes.

11
00:02:10,290 --> 00:02:14,550
She's uninjured, and perhaps because
 she now feels safe, she's fast asleep.

12
00:02:17,490 --> 00:02:21,580
Anyway, you and Mother were so cool, Father!

13
00:02:22,420 --> 00:02:23,950
What's this all of a sudden?

14
00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:26,540
Have you guys always been like that?

15
00:02:26,850 --> 00:02:33,070
Their power was every bit as 
astonishing as my father said it was!

16
00:02:33,070 --> 00:02:35,560
That's the first I'm hearing of this!

17
00:02:35,940 --> 00:02:37,460
Mother!

18
00:02:37,460 --> 00:02:39,600
Vint said that?

19
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:43,180
Oh, he should have just told me himself.

20
00:02:43,180 --> 00:02:45,290
Perhaps Vint is a bit shy, huh?

21
00:02:45,290 --> 00:02:47,640
I'm not sure... Perhaps so.

22
00:02:47,640 --> 00:02:53,360
Still, it's been so long that
 I wasn't certain how much force to use.

23
00:02:53,650 --> 00:02:57,550
Well, you can summon me anytime, you know?

24
00:02:58,570 --> 00:03:00,110
That's true.

25
00:03:00,110 --> 00:03:05,280
My skills will get rusty if I don't use spirit
magic with you once in a while, Ori.

26
00:03:05,930 --> 00:03:09,250
Were my parents this amazing in the past too?

27
00:03:09,470 --> 00:03:10,920
Oh, most certainly.

28
00:03:10,920 --> 00:03:14,500
Once, the knights were ordered 
to apprehend some bandits.

29
00:03:15,030 --> 00:03:20,310
The bandits were trying to use tamed 
wolves to harry our forces.

30
00:03:20,310 --> 00:03:21,630
Wolves?

31
00:03:21,930 --> 00:03:25,490
Yes. Lord Rovel, who caught on
 to our enemy's scheme,

32
00:03:25,490 --> 00:03:29,470
immediately summoned Lady Origin. And then...

33
00:03:29,470 --> 00:03:31,230
And then?!

34
00:03:37,170 --> 00:03:43,070
Those ferocious wolves turned as docile 
as puppies before Lady Origin.

35
00:03:43,390 --> 00:03:48,740
Next, Lord Rovel used spirit magic
 that was like a tornado

36
00:03:48,970 --> 00:03:51,810
to lift the bandits and wolves into the air,

37
00:03:51,810 --> 00:03:55,210
then slammed them back down 
to earth, immobilizing them.

38
00:03:55,510 --> 00:03:57,620
The poor wolves...

39
00:03:57,620 --> 00:04:00,920
Thanks to your parents, it was 
very easy to apprehend them.

40
00:04:00,920 --> 00:04:03,700
As expected from Lord Rovel and the queen!

41
00:04:03,700 --> 00:04:06,260
Wait, magic that was like a tornado?

42
00:04:06,890 --> 00:04:07,950
Father.

43
00:04:08,350 --> 00:04:14,280
You usually use ice magic, 
but you can use wind magic as well?

44
00:04:15,530 --> 00:04:17,770
I can, as long as Ori is nearby.

45
00:04:17,770 --> 00:04:21,230
She can conjure 
all of the elements, after all.

46
00:04:21,230 --> 00:04:22,890
Makes sense!

47
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:29,000
Besides, my pact with your mother is the
only reason I can use magic in the first place.

48
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,520
Oh, I see.

49
00:04:30,910 --> 00:04:35,080
But don't you go making pacts
 with just anybody, okay, Ellen?

50
00:04:35,720 --> 00:04:36,920
Yes, ma'am!

51
00:04:38,110 --> 00:04:41,180
Ellen, you don't have to make 
a pact with anyone, okay?

52
00:04:41,180 --> 00:04:42,130
What?

53
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:46,550
Goodness, Rovel. You're so narrow-minded.

54
00:04:46,550 --> 00:04:48,170
Come on!

55
00:04:48,170 --> 00:04:50,920
Father, I can't breathe!

56
00:04:52,230 --> 00:04:53,180
Come in.

57
00:04:55,080 --> 00:04:58,400
Lady Rafilia has awakened.

58
00:05:01,620 --> 00:05:02,690
Rafilia.

59
00:05:03,290 --> 00:05:04,510
Gadiel!

60
00:05:05,810 --> 00:05:07,570
I'm glad you're safe.

61
00:05:09,550 --> 00:05:10,390
Your Highness.

62
00:05:11,090 --> 00:05:12,970
Let us talk details tomorrow.

63
00:05:12,970 --> 00:05:16,000
Understood. Well then, if you'll excuse me.

64
00:05:16,520 --> 00:05:19,340
Gadiel, thank you for worrying about me.

65
00:05:19,940 --> 00:05:20,650
Sure.

66
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:34,020
So you're Ellen.

67
00:05:35,320 --> 00:05:38,260
Yes. It's nice to meet you, Rafi—

68
00:05:37,020 --> 00:05:38,260
It's all your fault!

69
00:05:38,260 --> 00:05:40,230
It's your fault I got put in this mess!

70
00:05:40,230 --> 00:05:41,470
You're horrible!

71
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:43,800
Rafilia.

72
00:05:43,800 --> 00:05:44,610
But—

73
00:05:44,840 --> 00:05:49,610
You were targeted because you were
already exchanging letters with the prince.

74
00:05:50,010 --> 00:05:51,710
Ellen had nothing to do with it.

75
00:05:53,060 --> 00:05:55,810
Why is it <i>always</i> like this?

76
00:05:56,120 --> 00:05:58,010
All people talk about is Ellen!

77
00:05:59,260 --> 00:06:03,340
I'm a daughter of the Vankreift 
family too, you know?

78
00:06:03,820 --> 00:06:06,870
Is that... how you've felt all this time?

79
00:06:09,080 --> 00:06:11,740
You got a problem with me or something?!

80
00:06:11,740 --> 00:06:18,340
What? I was just trying to help out 
the Vankreift family for my father.

81
00:06:18,340 --> 00:06:22,920
And... I'm really sorry about what happened.

82
00:06:23,720 --> 00:06:27,480
Hmph! Gadiel said he wanted 
to see you too, but...

83
00:06:28,740 --> 00:06:31,410
Are you really the same age as me?

84
00:06:31,410 --> 00:06:32,200
Huh?

85
00:06:35,880 --> 00:06:39,020
You're small in more ways than one.

86
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:42,170
What do you mean?

87
00:06:42,670 --> 00:06:43,660
Hmph!

88
00:06:47,380 --> 00:06:49,940
Th-They'll get bigger!

89
00:06:49,940 --> 00:06:54,050
What, starting now? 
Don't ya think it's a bit late for that?

90
00:06:54,740 --> 00:06:57,510
They'll grow big...

91
00:07:02,220 --> 00:07:05,880
Your mother's are huge,
so you'll be fine, Ellen.

92
00:07:05,880 --> 00:07:08,390
Father!

93
00:07:10,060 --> 00:07:14,050
There, there. Yep, nothing to worry about.

94
00:07:16,390 --> 00:07:20,800
A mere human speaking 
so rudely to the princess...

95
00:07:20,800 --> 00:07:22,380
I'll remember that.

96
00:07:31,900 --> 00:07:34,810
Ellen, don't worry about it
 and get some rest.

97
00:07:34,810 --> 00:07:35,890
But...

98
00:07:36,540 --> 00:07:37,560
Princess!

99
00:07:38,110 --> 00:07:40,930
Shall I go tear that little girl to shreds?

100
00:07:40,930 --> 00:07:42,980
Van?! No, don't do that!

101
00:07:42,980 --> 00:07:45,690
Rafilia is my cousin.

102
00:07:46,270 --> 00:07:47,900
Your cousin, you say?

103
00:07:47,900 --> 00:07:51,610
Yes, so don't be mad.

104
00:07:53,630 --> 00:07:55,330
I shall do my best.

105
00:07:55,810 --> 00:07:56,700
Oh, I know!

106
00:07:59,180 --> 00:08:00,250
Here, my princess!

107
00:08:00,590 --> 00:08:02,130
Indulge in my fluff as you please!

108
00:08:03,140 --> 00:08:05,220
Van!

109
00:08:14,590 --> 00:08:16,220
Oh, fine already.

110
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:19,270
Join in, Father. Let's enjoy it together.

111
00:08:19,270 --> 00:08:20,640
All right!

112
00:08:20,640 --> 00:08:25,100
Fluffy, fluffy, fluffy, fluffy, fluffy fluff!

113
00:08:20,640 --> 00:08:25,100
FLUFFY FLUFFY FLUFFY

114
00:08:28,710 --> 00:08:30,820
I want to grow up fast...

115
00:08:33,490 --> 00:08:38,010
Hey, Ellen. Why are you 
in such a hurry to grow up?

116
00:08:38,870 --> 00:08:42,430
There's no way to stop growing, 
even as a spirit.

117
00:08:42,980 --> 00:08:45,300
You'll be an adult eventually, no matter what.

118
00:08:45,990 --> 00:08:49,090
So what's wrong with things as they are now?

119
00:08:50,030 --> 00:08:51,770
You're making your dad feel lonely.

120
00:08:52,730 --> 00:08:56,550
When you grow up, 
you'll be leaving my side, you know?

121
00:08:56,550 --> 00:08:59,250
That's... That's...

122
00:08:57,910 --> 00:08:59,250
Father?

123
00:08:59,250 --> 00:09:01,160
I don't <i>want that</i>!

124
00:09:01,160 --> 00:09:06,270
Ellen, please don't <i>ever</i> get married!

125
00:09:11,310 --> 00:09:13,890
Ouch... That hurt, Ellen.

126
00:09:13,890 --> 00:09:16,910
Father, just what's gotten into you?

127
00:09:18,990 --> 00:09:20,370
Do you feel better?

128
00:09:22,250 --> 00:09:24,330
Yes, completely.

129
00:09:26,830 --> 00:09:31,250
I'm happy to have you 
and Mother as my parents.

130
00:09:36,140 --> 00:09:37,130
How's Ellen?

131
00:09:37,130 --> 00:09:39,370
She cried herself to sleep.

132
00:09:39,370 --> 00:09:43,160
My apologies for Rafilia. 
To have spoken to Ellen like that...

133
00:09:43,160 --> 00:09:48,180
Yeah, well, Ellen thought nothing of it.
Except for the whole size thing.

134
00:09:50,130 --> 00:09:52,810
Listen, I'm sorry.

135
00:09:52,810 --> 00:09:57,020
You daughter got dragged into all this
because of us and the royal family.

136
00:09:57,020 --> 00:09:59,610
No, think nothing of it.

137
00:09:59,610 --> 00:10:02,330
In fact, I think things may have
 turned out for the better.

138
00:10:03,570 --> 00:10:05,260
It's a bit of an odd story,

139
00:10:05,660 --> 00:10:10,130
but this incident has finally made me realize
why Rafilia's been so rebellious.

140
00:10:10,460 --> 00:10:12,970
I now understand how she feels.

141
00:10:13,330 --> 00:10:16,970
Well, I'm certain it's only 
the tip of the iceberg, but...

142
00:10:17,730 --> 00:10:19,180
That's important.

143
00:10:20,060 --> 00:10:21,220
Yes.

144
00:10:24,970 --> 00:10:27,150
Anyway, that was all exhausting!

145
00:10:27,150 --> 00:10:28,890
It's been some time, hasn't it?

146
00:10:30,930 --> 00:10:35,070
I wanted to join in and let loose myself,
 I'll have you know!

147
00:10:44,300 --> 00:10:48,400
To think I'd be guarding the 
princess with a brat like you.

148
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:49,920
Are you displeased I was chosen?

149
00:10:50,200 --> 00:10:55,810
Displeased, you say? You bet I am. 
What can a brat like you even do?

150
00:10:55,810 --> 00:10:59,090
I'm honored to be able 
to work with a great spirit.

151
00:10:59,440 --> 00:11:01,700
I cannot go to the spirit world,

152
00:11:01,700 --> 00:11:05,500
so I think it's only natural that you 
were selected to protect Lady Ellen.

153
00:11:05,500 --> 00:11:06,890
But of course.

154
00:11:06,890 --> 00:11:11,390
However, I believe that my desire
 to protect her is no different than yours.

155
00:11:13,570 --> 00:11:15,820
So I'm pleased to be working with you.

156
00:11:17,350 --> 00:11:18,650
What is this?

157
00:11:19,010 --> 00:11:23,530
It's the customary gesture humans use 
to begin good working relationships.

158
00:11:24,060 --> 00:11:26,370
Why greet me with a human custom?

159
00:11:26,370 --> 00:11:29,850
If you plan on taking on a human form, 
you'd do well to remember it.

160
00:11:42,500 --> 00:11:43,400
Amazing!

161
00:11:43,400 --> 00:11:47,470
Hey, stop that! My paws 
are for the princess only!

162
00:11:48,280 --> 00:11:50,590
This is how humans greet each other.

163
00:11:50,590 --> 00:11:51,670
Quit lying!

164
00:11:59,890 --> 00:12:01,860
Prince Gadiel has arrived.

165
00:12:04,840 --> 00:12:08,770
Once again, I thank you
 for your cooperation yesterday.

166
00:12:09,330 --> 00:12:12,290
Rafilia has returned safely thanks to you.

167
00:12:12,990 --> 00:12:13,920
Right.

168
00:12:14,260 --> 00:12:15,240
Your Highness.

169
00:12:15,650 --> 00:12:18,330
About this letter Rafilia received...

170
00:12:18,820 --> 00:12:21,340
What are your thoughts on it?

171
00:12:24,680 --> 00:12:30,040
It reads: "I will be visiting the 
Vankreift domain on a mission.

172
00:12:30,720 --> 00:12:32,470
If it's all right, could we meet?"

173
00:12:34,030 --> 00:12:37,900
You're already aware that this 
was sent from the royal family, yes?

174
00:12:38,510 --> 00:12:40,360
As for the contents of the letter...

175
00:12:41,250 --> 00:12:45,340
You must already have some idea 
of who was responsible for it, don't you?

176
00:12:46,760 --> 00:12:48,260
It could only be His Majesty.

177
00:12:48,750 --> 00:12:53,330
I told him I was exchanging
 letters with Rafilia, after all.

178
00:12:53,630 --> 00:12:55,040
With this knowledge, His Majesty

179
00:12:55,690 --> 00:12:59,650
sent you on a mission
 to investigate the Vankreift domain.

180
00:13:01,340 --> 00:13:04,460
His Majesty wanted to learn more 
about our medicine

181
00:13:04,460 --> 00:13:08,790
by involving you with me and my father,
 all using Rafilia as bait.

182
00:13:08,790 --> 00:13:09,970
That can't be...

183
00:13:09,970 --> 00:13:14,850
Prince Gadiel, this is how 
King Ravisel operates.

184
00:13:15,650 --> 00:13:18,060
It's why I despise that man.

185
00:13:21,740 --> 00:13:25,300
Well, this will serve as a test for you.

186
00:13:27,160 --> 00:13:30,090
Rafilia was abducted on His Majesty's orders.

187
00:13:30,840 --> 00:13:32,620
That is how we see it.

188
00:13:32,620 --> 00:13:36,580
You're wrong! Those people had
 no connection to the royal family!

189
00:13:36,580 --> 00:13:39,580
Given the situation, it's only 
natural for us to believe they did.

190
00:13:40,430 --> 00:13:42,550
Or do you have some kind of proof?

191
00:13:42,550 --> 00:13:43,760
Either way, we...

192
00:13:43,760 --> 00:13:47,750
You didn't know. 
That is what you were about to claim, yes?

193
00:13:48,280 --> 00:13:52,170
Nevertheless, wouldn't you agree this is an 
issue between us and the royal family?

194
00:13:52,660 --> 00:13:56,180
Well... Yes. It is.

195
00:13:56,770 --> 00:13:58,850
I'm glad to see that 
we have an understanding.

196
00:13:59,310 --> 00:14:02,170
Now, let us move on
 to the subject of the medicine.

197
00:14:02,690 --> 00:14:05,780
As promised, I will hand it 
over to you, Your Highness.

198
00:14:06,090 --> 00:14:07,700
Father, the medicine.

199
00:14:11,950 --> 00:14:16,270
You can examine it, administer it,
 do as you please with it.

200
00:14:17,290 --> 00:14:20,000
Is there any way you could
 teach us to make it?

201
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:21,660
Please, I beg you.

202
00:14:21,660 --> 00:14:23,000
I cannot.

203
00:14:23,730 --> 00:14:24,840
Don't say that.

204
00:14:24,840 --> 00:14:28,530
I cannot give the royal family 
the details of the medicine.

205
00:14:29,160 --> 00:14:31,550
Even if I were to share with you 
how to make it,

206
00:14:31,550 --> 00:14:33,810
you would not understand.

207
00:14:34,620 --> 00:14:35,890
What do you mean by that?

208
00:14:36,260 --> 00:14:39,780
This medicine cannot
 be produced in the human world.

209
00:14:39,780 --> 00:14:40,350
What?

210
00:14:40,740 --> 00:14:41,560
What did you say?

211
00:14:42,260 --> 00:14:48,030
Granted, that doesn't mean spirits who live 
in the spirit world can make it either.

212
00:14:48,030 --> 00:14:51,640
Then what on earth is this medicine?!

213
00:14:52,700 --> 00:14:53,910
I cannot tell you.

214
00:14:55,850 --> 00:14:59,900
Why not try asking your spirit?

215
00:15:00,450 --> 00:15:02,470
That's why you brought it, no?

216
00:15:03,080 --> 00:15:03,710
Your Highness?

217
00:15:09,900 --> 00:15:11,460
Ashute, if you could.

218
00:15:15,310 --> 00:15:16,090
Well?

219
00:15:18,920 --> 00:15:20,100
You don't know?

220
00:15:20,600 --> 00:15:23,560
Hue, this is something that 
doesn't exist in the human world.

221
00:15:24,690 --> 00:15:26,780
So is it a medicine from the spirit world?

222
00:15:27,690 --> 00:15:30,600
Spirits don't need medicine.

223
00:15:31,630 --> 00:15:34,330
Then what about the ingredients?
Are they of the spirit world?

224
00:15:34,330 --> 00:15:38,600
Don't think so. Ashu has never seen them before.

225
00:15:39,660 --> 00:15:41,790
Then what in the world...

226
00:15:41,790 --> 00:15:44,700
You cannot make that medicine.

227
00:15:45,310 --> 00:15:47,380
We will supply it to you.

228
00:15:47,950 --> 00:15:49,190
That's all there is to it.

229
00:15:49,190 --> 00:15:50,380
That can't be...

230
00:15:51,270 --> 00:15:52,590
Let us move along.

231
00:15:53,190 --> 00:15:56,930
The medicine I just handed you
 is called an antibiotic.

232
00:15:57,300 --> 00:15:59,620
It kills the root of the disease,

233
00:15:59,620 --> 00:16:04,060
but at the same time, it also kills 
the good bacteria within the stomach.

234
00:16:04,400 --> 00:16:08,730
You must keep taking the 
medicine until the disease is gone,

235
00:16:08,730 --> 00:16:12,050
but in exchange,
 you may get terrible diarrhea.

236
00:16:12,050 --> 00:16:14,660
This is what's known as a side effect.

237
00:16:15,530 --> 00:16:17,370
A side effect?

238
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:20,330
Many things can cause illness.

239
00:16:20,330 --> 00:16:23,000
A healer must determine which
based on the presented symptoms

240
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:25,530
and prescribe various medications.

241
00:16:26,850 --> 00:16:29,430
Give thorough instructions
as to the precautions of each,

242
00:16:29,430 --> 00:16:32,050
and ensure proper hygiene in the future.

243
00:16:32,470 --> 00:16:34,200
Without these preventative measures,

244
00:16:34,200 --> 00:16:36,550
we won't be able
 to maintain the medicine supply,

245
00:16:41,980 --> 00:16:42,930
Hume.

246
00:16:43,150 --> 00:16:44,690
Y-Yes?

247
00:16:44,970 --> 00:16:49,720
Would you please talk to our house healer
about how to handle the medicine?

248
00:16:49,720 --> 00:16:54,770
Take all due care, as medicine can 
become poison when handled incorrectly.

249
00:16:55,580 --> 00:16:57,070
Understood.

250
00:16:57,460 --> 00:17:00,180
Pawpaw, please show him there
 if you'd be so kind.

251
00:17:00,550 --> 00:17:02,050
It would be my pleasure.

252
00:17:02,500 --> 00:17:04,790
Sir Hume, right this way.

253
00:17:04,790 --> 00:17:05,530
Okay.

254
00:17:09,670 --> 00:17:10,550
Your Highness.

255
00:17:12,130 --> 00:17:15,610
We've given this first batch to you 
in accordance with our promise,

256
00:17:16,140 --> 00:17:19,350
but we will expect payment
 for any future deliveries.

257
00:17:19,700 --> 00:17:20,810
What?

258
00:17:21,170 --> 00:17:22,890
This is the deal we're offering.

259
00:17:24,230 --> 00:17:29,480
My apologies. I would like to consult 
His Majesty on the matter first.

260
00:17:29,480 --> 00:17:30,830
That's fine.

261
00:17:31,260 --> 00:17:36,260
However, please inform him that we expect
terms that are satisfactory to us.

262
00:17:37,950 --> 00:17:38,910
I shall.

263
00:17:39,890 --> 00:17:42,660
Now then, let us return
 to the original matter.

264
00:17:43,130 --> 00:17:46,540
We shall be the ones to deal 
with the men who kidnapped Rafilia.

265
00:17:46,540 --> 00:17:48,710
Wait! We can't allow that!

266
00:17:48,710 --> 00:17:53,420
Did you not state that they have
 no connection to the royal family?

267
00:17:54,970 --> 00:18:00,560
My father says that His Majesty likely 
has proof that he isn't involved,

268
00:18:00,560 --> 00:18:02,300
whether or not we hand them over.

269
00:18:02,930 --> 00:18:05,730
So he should take no issue with this.

270
00:18:06,070 --> 00:18:07,460
Well, that's...

271
00:18:07,460 --> 00:18:12,410
I already warned you
 to be prepared for what's to come.

272
00:18:13,690 --> 00:18:17,170
Your Highness, 
please relay this to His Majesty:

273
00:18:17,780 --> 00:18:21,410
You will regret ever touching my family.

274
00:18:22,050 --> 00:18:23,630
That is all.

275
00:18:29,110 --> 00:18:30,130
P-Please wait!

276
00:18:31,840 --> 00:18:33,170
What is it?

277
00:18:37,180 --> 00:18:38,470
What is it?

278
00:18:39,790 --> 00:18:41,850
You said you'd hear me out.

279
00:18:44,110 --> 00:18:49,350
If we manage to find Rafilia safely, 
I ask that you please hear me out.

280
00:18:50,170 --> 00:18:51,600
I believe I had your word.

281
00:18:52,920 --> 00:18:54,830
Here, right now?

282
00:18:54,830 --> 00:19:00,670
If not now, I have a feeling I'll never
 have another chance to speak with you.

283
00:19:05,030 --> 00:19:08,510
Would all of you please give us a moment?

284
00:19:09,090 --> 00:19:12,170
Ellen, you plan on talking to him alone?

285
00:19:12,170 --> 00:19:14,340
Is this something I can't stay for?

286
00:19:16,030 --> 00:19:18,380
Father, please.

287
00:19:22,680 --> 00:19:24,050
All right.

288
00:19:24,820 --> 00:19:27,140
Listen, I'll say this one more time to be sure.

289
00:19:27,700 --> 00:19:29,640
Do not approach Ellen.

290
00:19:30,810 --> 00:19:31,900
I know.

291
00:19:40,630 --> 00:19:44,200
Ellen, what we... What the royal 
family did to the spirits...

292
00:19:44,200 --> 00:19:46,990
Your Highness, you are part
 of that royal family.

293
00:19:48,730 --> 00:19:52,400
Your ancestors did something 
they shouldn't have.

294
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:55,960
However, as a royal yourself, I'm sure that

295
00:19:55,960 --> 00:19:59,370
you understand the reason
 behind their actions.

296
00:19:59,950 --> 00:20:05,640
At the time, the royal family sought
the spirits' power to protect the country.

297
00:20:05,880 --> 00:20:08,890
But we still shouldn't have gone so far.

298
00:20:09,740 --> 00:20:14,020
If you understand, then you of all people 
should not be apologizing for it.

299
00:20:14,590 --> 00:20:17,480
What? How could you say that?

300
00:20:18,020 --> 00:20:21,690
Your ancestors had no regrets.

301
00:20:23,010 --> 00:20:24,720
Whatever it meant for the royal family,

302
00:20:24,720 --> 00:20:29,110
they intended to save their people from 
the Monster Tempest two hundred years ago.

303
00:20:29,610 --> 00:20:32,510
And that is how they went about it.

304
00:20:32,510 --> 00:20:34,210
Still, the spirits didn't deserve...

305
00:20:36,280 --> 00:20:40,380
They must have been so desperate 
that it was their only option.

306
00:20:42,260 --> 00:20:47,170
There is no undoing the sorrow
 of the spirits sacrificed.

307
00:20:47,580 --> 00:20:51,250
Because even though it is a thing
 of the past for you royals,

308
00:20:52,110 --> 00:20:57,640
to the eternal spirits, 
it is as if it were only yesterday.

309
00:20:58,030 --> 00:21:00,100
Still, I...

310
00:21:01,990 --> 00:21:05,530
Your Highness, I have warned you.

311
00:21:06,030 --> 00:21:07,450
You had best be prepared.

312
00:21:08,840 --> 00:21:09,660
Yes.

313
00:21:10,220 --> 00:21:13,250
I'm certain His Majesty heard 
those cursed cries as well.

314
00:21:13,660 --> 00:21:17,430
But in spite of that, he's dared
 to lay a hand on my family.

315
00:21:19,620 --> 00:21:21,780
The spreading of the disease 
is gaining momentum.

316
00:21:23,220 --> 00:21:26,890
Soon the royal capital will likely 
be thrown into turmoil.

317
00:21:28,140 --> 00:21:31,940
King Ravisel has taken us too lightly.

318
00:21:32,420 --> 00:21:37,800
After all he's done, do not think
 for a moment you will have our aid.

319
00:21:39,740 --> 00:21:41,690
This is our final warning.

320
00:21:42,280 --> 00:21:45,610
Please do not make contact with us ever again.

321
00:21:46,150 --> 00:21:49,290
But... I...

322
00:21:50,730 --> 00:21:51,830
I...

323
00:21:56,770 --> 00:21:59,430
There's nothing more to talk about.

324
00:22:01,460 --> 00:22:02,390
Ellen!

325
00:22:09,370 --> 00:22:13,730
I just... want to talk to you.

326
00:22:15,270 --> 00:22:19,160
Am I... not allowed even that?

327
00:22:21,170 --> 00:22:24,630
Translation: Yukari Murase-Louden

328
00:22:24,920 --> 00:22:28,340
Editing: Riley Dalton

329
00:22:28,680 --> 00:22:31,850
